ong because look I had a very  idealistic view of that life when I came  in I was going oh I'm gonna be part of  something my father's part of you know  this Brotherhood among men it was  exhilarating and I took it extremely  seriously  so leaving that life was was very very  difficult it really was I mean sometimes  you know even even at a moment I mean I  feel it today every wata be out of your  mind to me to be in that life you're  going to jail you're going down one way  the other at one point in time  especially it was too late for me I  became too high-profile once you got  that bullseye on your back you got that  target they'll never let you go they got  all the time all the money all the  resources so they're gonna get you when  they do get you it's over that's it  treachery free kids yeah I got a you  know a wife to them 34 years here we  live out in Southern Cal I got seven  great kids you know three from my first  marriage but they all love each other  which is great look I live a good  lifestyle I mean you know I'm speaking  all over the world having a a positive  impact on people being a source of  encouragement and hope which is  extremely gratifying you know I really  learned in my life it really is better  to give than receive you get a better  feeling out of it you know and what else  can you give me I've gotten everything  just about my life but it motivates me  keeps me going very fortunate I am a  person of faith you know and look and my  faith has played a major role it's  without God in my life I don't think I'd  be sitting here now I mean I know that  for a fact so you know and things I've  had my challenges and my struggles don't  get me wrong and you know I didn't get a  lobotomy when I became a person of faith  I still have tendencies where I could  jump back in and mob life for a second  but I try not to and I got the right  people around me to keep  be accountable so you know it's all  working out  excellent what a great great story  than